# Port progress docs

- **Start with** [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-current.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-current.md) — next steps, constraints.
- Skim [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-remaining.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-remaining.md) for **unported / stub / harness** surface so slices stay focused.
- Canonical **continue** prompt + workflow: [`.cursor/prompts/continue-nethack-port.md`](../prompts/continue-nethack-port.md).
- Use [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-progress.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-progress.md) for **deep** module tables and long-form analysis only when needed (token-heavy).
- New dated changelog rows go in [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-changelog-archive.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-changelog-archive.md); keep the stub in `c-to-js-port-progress.md` short.

Contest integrity: port from **C** in `nethack-c/upstream/`; no session trace memorization; do not edit frozen `js/isaac64.js`, `js/terminal.js`, `js/storage.js`.

After each meaningful slice: **`git commit`** (one commit; conventional message) per [`.cursor/prompts/continue-nethack-port.md`](../prompts/continue-nethack-port.md).
